1
00:01:28,464 --> 00:01:29,590
I feel like

2
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:32,885
we have something to say to each other.

3
00:01:33,677 --> 00:01:35,554
Yes, we do.

4
00:01:36,847 --> 00:01:37,765
Back then,

5
00:01:39,058 --> 00:01:41,769
why did you leave without hearing me out?

6
00:01:42,186 --> 00:01:44,814
Anyone could tell
you were making a confession of love.

7
00:01:44,897 --> 00:01:46,732
I did make a confession of love

8
00:01:48,359 --> 00:01:49,568
for you.

9
00:01:52,029 --> 00:01:53,656
-What?
-I mean,

10
00:01:53,739 --> 00:01:56,742
why would you get upset and leave
before hearing everything?

11
00:01:56,826 --> 00:01:59,495
-You clearly confessed…
-I have feelings for…

12
00:01:59,578 --> 00:02:02,581
I like Yoon Yi-jun.

13
00:02:10,798 --> 00:02:12,633
It was for me?

14
00:02:13,801 --> 00:02:15,845
I had no idea.
I misunderstood the situation.

15
00:02:23,644 --> 00:02:24,520
I'm sorry.

16
00:02:32,027 --> 00:02:33,112
The bus is here.

17
00:02:34,780 --> 00:02:35,823
Come with me.

18
00:02:36,323 --> 00:02:37,199
With you?

19
00:02:39,785 --> 00:02:40,911
For two.

20
00:02:41,662 --> 00:02:42,705
Really?

21
00:02:46,959 --> 00:02:48,419
Sitting in the back is the best.

22
00:02:49,044 --> 00:02:50,004
I see.

23
00:02:51,589 --> 00:02:53,632
-Have you ever been on a bus?
-Of course.

24
00:02:57,011 --> 00:02:59,430
-Get some rest.
-You're going home already?

25
00:03:00,139 --> 00:03:02,182
Since you're here, why don't you come in?

26
00:03:02,266 --> 00:03:03,183
Wait,

27
00:03:04,310 --> 00:03:05,311
is this something like

28
00:03:06,896 --> 00:03:08,981
"Do you want to come in
for instant noodles?"

29
00:03:09,231 --> 00:03:10,399
Not at all.

30
00:03:10,900 --> 00:03:12,818
In the movie where they said that,

31
00:03:12,902 --> 00:03:14,403
an adult man and woman

32
00:03:14,486 --> 00:03:16,447
-ended up…
-Ended up?

33
00:03:18,032 --> 00:03:21,118
I didn't even have that in mind.
What are you saying?

34
00:03:21,619 --> 00:03:23,871
-My gosh…
-Yes, you did.

35
00:03:24,330 --> 00:03:25,414
You clearly did.

36
00:03:25,497 --> 00:03:27,958
Otherwise, why would your ears turn red?

37
00:03:28,292 --> 00:03:29,460
They're not red.

38
00:03:30,169 --> 00:03:31,712
I don't even eat instant noodles.

39
00:03:32,671 --> 00:03:33,797
That's a bummer.

40
00:03:35,215 --> 00:03:37,343
Because I had a lot of things in mind.

41
00:03:37,801 --> 00:03:38,636
What?

42
00:03:39,219 --> 00:03:40,512
I want to go to cafés

43
00:03:40,596 --> 00:03:43,474
and watch movies with you,
not as Managing Director Yoon,

44
00:03:43,557 --> 00:03:44,892
-but as Yi-jun.
-Right.

45
00:03:45,351 --> 00:03:48,479
I wanted to do normal things
that other people do.

46
00:03:48,562 --> 00:03:50,314
-I see.
-I have a list

47
00:03:51,065 --> 00:03:52,399
with about 150 items.

48
00:03:52,483 --> 00:03:54,652
That's a lot of things you wanted to try.

49
00:03:56,779 --> 00:03:58,864
-Let's hear them.
-This is one of them.

50
00:03:59,490 --> 00:04:02,868
Safely escorting you home as Yi-jun,
not as the managing director.

51
00:04:03,285 --> 00:04:04,578
That's it?

52
00:04:05,996 --> 00:04:07,498
-What else?
-Let's see.

53
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:09,166
I have so many.

54
00:04:09,708 --> 00:04:11,919
Riding bicycles together,

55
00:04:12,252 --> 00:04:13,879
going to good restaurants,

56
00:04:14,129 --> 00:04:15,965
taking lots of pictures,

57
00:04:16,256 --> 00:04:17,758
and going on a trip together.

58
00:04:19,218 --> 00:04:21,345
Speaking of which,
do you want to go tomorrow?

59
00:04:21,720 --> 00:04:23,472
-Tomorrow?
-Let's do it.

60
00:04:25,224 --> 00:04:30,020
Although I'm busy even on the weekends
that 24 hours isn't enough…

61
00:04:30,104 --> 00:04:32,106
-Are you refusing?
-I said "although."

62
00:04:32,189 --> 00:04:33,524
Don't cut me off.

63
00:04:34,608 --> 00:04:37,027
Anyway, I'll make time for you.

64
00:04:40,990 --> 00:04:41,949
See you tomorrow.

65
00:04:43,909 --> 00:04:44,785
Okay.

66
00:04:49,331 --> 00:04:50,207
See you tomorrow!

67
00:04:59,550 --> 00:05:01,760
EPISODE 10

68
00:05:27,911 --> 00:05:29,663
I should

69
00:05:30,080 --> 00:05:31,874
at least wear the dry-cleaned one.

70
00:05:35,085 --> 00:05:37,171
But I'm not going to work.

71
00:05:38,589 --> 00:05:39,631
This one.

72
00:05:44,011 --> 00:05:45,095
This is cute.

73
00:05:46,263 --> 00:05:47,264
Okay.

74
00:05:47,347 --> 00:05:48,182
No!

75
00:05:51,143 --> 00:05:52,269
This won't do.

76
00:05:53,187 --> 00:05:54,188
This won't do either!

77
00:05:57,024 --> 00:05:58,692
I look too dressed up!

78
00:05:58,776 --> 00:06:02,529
I came early in the morning
to watch this eyesore.

79
00:06:02,613 --> 00:06:05,115
How rewarding is this?

80
00:06:06,033 --> 00:06:08,786
She has 150 things
she wants to do with me.

81
00:06:10,079 --> 00:06:13,165
Since it's our first date, we should go
somewhere abroad that's close.

82
00:06:13,248 --> 00:06:16,502
You're not about to suggest
taking the private jet, are you?

83
00:06:16,585 --> 00:06:18,504
Is going abroad a bit too much?

84
00:06:18,587 --> 00:06:20,547
Then we'll stay within the country.

85
00:06:20,631 --> 00:06:21,715
A beach in Jeju Island?

86
00:06:21,799 --> 00:06:24,134
Watching fireworks on a yacht?

87
00:06:24,218 --> 00:06:26,595
You guys will freeze your butts off.
How exciting!

88
00:06:27,346 --> 00:06:28,972
We can do that when it gets warmer.

89
00:06:29,515 --> 00:06:32,184
I can't go empty-handed.
I'll buy her a small gift.

90
00:06:32,267 --> 00:06:35,270
Don't tell me you'll buy everything
you see at a boutique

91
00:06:35,354 --> 00:06:37,981
and tell her "I just picked this up."
Gosh, Mr. Yoon!

92
00:06:38,065 --> 00:06:41,568
I know you're a handful,
but you can't go throwing money around.

93
00:06:41,652 --> 00:06:44,780
I want to look cool on our first date!

94
00:06:44,863 --> 00:06:47,407
Shouldn't you do something
that'll bring you closer?

95
00:06:47,491 --> 00:06:50,244
Something casual and fun
where you can talk a lot.

96
00:06:50,327 --> 00:06:51,370
Get out.

97
00:06:52,788 --> 00:06:54,665
You're lecturing me when you got dumped?

98
00:07:01,338 --> 00:07:02,172
Not yet.

99
00:07:02,714 --> 00:07:04,925
Please let me get ready to go on a date.

100
00:07:05,008 --> 00:07:07,010
Unlike you, I wasn't rejected.

101
00:07:07,094 --> 00:07:08,470
I haven't been dumped yet!

102
00:07:08,887 --> 00:07:10,472
I still have a chance!

103
00:07:24,236 --> 00:07:25,404
Do I have everything?

104
00:07:25,487 --> 00:07:27,072
I'm sure you do.

105
00:07:27,156 --> 00:07:30,284
No need to see me out.
Review the marriage termination agreement.

106
00:07:30,868 --> 00:07:34,037
We agreed on everything beforehand.
Plus, you already signed it.

107
00:07:34,121 --> 00:07:35,539
Why do you think I called you?

108
00:07:37,166 --> 00:07:39,543
There are two ways
to piss off a good lawyer.

109
00:07:39,626 --> 00:07:42,087
One, making them review a contract
that's been finalized.

110
00:07:42,171 --> 00:07:44,673
Two, nitpicking a flawless contract that…

111
00:07:45,132 --> 00:07:47,551
Hang on, did you prepare that?
Where's Manager Choi?

112
00:07:50,179 --> 00:07:51,013
She quit.

113
00:07:52,514 --> 00:07:53,640
Mr. Yoon.

114
00:07:55,184 --> 00:07:56,476
I'm sorry, sir.

115
00:08:06,195 --> 00:08:08,155
She sold my information to Na-jung.

116
00:08:08,238 --> 00:08:10,449
She saw the gardener
tampering with the milk.

117
00:08:12,242 --> 00:08:14,077
When will Na-jung stop this madness?

118
00:08:16,622 --> 00:08:18,957
So what are the good ways
to piss off a good lawyer?

119
00:08:19,374 --> 00:08:21,043
Right. Two, nitpicking--

120
00:08:21,126 --> 00:08:22,044
That's interesting.

121
00:08:22,127 --> 00:08:23,587
-I'm still talking. Hey.
-Bye.

122
00:08:23,670 --> 00:08:25,297
Stay here and review the document.

123
00:08:25,380 --> 00:08:29,843
Two, nitpicking a flawless contract
for no good reason!

124
00:08:49,404 --> 00:08:50,864
GROOM
KIM GYU-MIN

125
00:08:50,948 --> 00:08:52,407
BRIDE
LEE HYE-JUNG

126
00:08:53,617 --> 00:08:55,410
What was I supposed to do? I was worried!

127
00:08:55,494 --> 00:08:59,289
I'm terrified that you'll put yourself
in danger by knowing too much!

128
00:09:02,209 --> 00:09:03,794
Did you not have enough?

129
00:09:03,877 --> 00:09:05,462
Do you want to trust a man again?

130
00:09:06,338 --> 00:09:07,798
Being deceived once is enough.

131
00:09:14,012 --> 00:09:14,930
Captain.

132
00:09:15,889 --> 00:09:18,392
Yoon Yi-jun broke off the marriage
because of me.

133
00:09:19,643 --> 00:09:21,395
You're driving me crazy.

134
00:09:21,478 --> 00:09:24,564
You think you're a heroine, don't you?

135
00:09:24,648 --> 00:09:28,610
Yes, that's why
I'm responsible for him now.

136
00:09:29,027 --> 00:09:30,362
Goodness gracious.

137
00:09:30,445 --> 00:09:33,865
I'm serious. There's no turning back now.

138
00:09:33,949 --> 00:09:36,535
I really want to catch Na Man-seok.

139
00:09:36,618 --> 00:09:38,078
I'll take down the jerk

140
00:09:38,620 --> 00:09:39,913
who hurt Yoon Yi-jun.

141
00:09:42,249 --> 00:09:43,959
Hey, Jae-hee.

142
00:09:44,042 --> 00:09:46,878
I'll get down on my knees and beg.

143
00:09:46,962 --> 00:09:48,922
You told me on the first day we met

144
00:09:49,006 --> 00:09:50,590
to catch the culprit no matter what.

145
00:09:50,674 --> 00:09:54,303
I engraved those words on my heart.

146
00:09:54,386 --> 00:09:57,556
I was just putting on a show
in front of you guys.

147
00:09:57,639 --> 00:09:59,266
You didn't have to take it to heart.

148
00:09:59,349 --> 00:10:02,019
I already did, regardless of
if you were pretending or not.

149
00:10:02,728 --> 00:10:05,355
Please call off the withdrawal.

150
00:10:06,148 --> 00:10:08,108
I'll reveal the truth to Mr. Yoon

151
00:10:08,191 --> 00:10:10,569
and ask for his cooperation. Please.

152
00:10:32,924 --> 00:10:33,842
Open wide.

153
00:10:56,865 --> 00:10:58,200
Do a V sign.

154
00:11:21,181 --> 00:11:23,141
I guess you weren't taking a photo.

155
00:11:23,225 --> 00:11:25,477
I wasn't meaning to take a photo.

156
00:11:26,395 --> 00:11:29,314
They asked me
to test the camera performance.

157
00:11:29,773 --> 00:11:31,525
They could've tested it themselves.

158
00:11:31,608 --> 00:11:33,026
Wait a second.

159
00:11:37,030 --> 00:11:38,073
You look cool today.

160
00:11:38,990 --> 00:11:39,908
Really?

161
00:11:41,410 --> 00:11:44,996
It's not like I dressed up
especially for today.

162
00:11:46,164 --> 00:11:47,791
It's a bit of a shame.

163
00:11:48,333 --> 00:11:49,501
You'll be changing anyway.

164
00:11:50,085 --> 00:11:51,002
What?

165
00:11:53,171 --> 00:11:54,631
Please get changed.

166
00:11:54,714 --> 00:11:55,924
What are we doing here?

167
00:11:56,007 --> 00:11:58,510
-That's the men's locker room.
-Do I really have to?

168
00:11:58,593 --> 00:12:00,053
I've always wanted to do this.

169
00:12:00,137 --> 00:12:01,221
No.

170
00:12:02,013 --> 00:12:03,807
I don't think this is a good idea.

171
00:12:03,890 --> 00:12:06,268
What if something happens
while I'm not around?

172
00:12:06,351 --> 00:12:10,439
Why do we have to do this
on our first date?

173
00:12:10,522 --> 00:12:12,023
Fine!

174
00:12:12,899 --> 00:12:13,942
Listen to me first.

175
00:12:15,152 --> 00:12:16,319
So,

176
00:12:16,403 --> 00:12:20,240
I want to do things other couples do
instead of this.

177
00:12:20,323 --> 00:12:22,284
There are so many normal things we can do!

178
00:12:22,367 --> 00:12:24,786
Other couples do this as well.

179
00:12:24,870 --> 00:12:26,997
And I woke up early
to get ready for today.

180
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:28,081
Fine.

181
00:12:29,499 --> 00:12:30,584
What about this?

182
00:12:31,209 --> 00:12:32,127
This?

183
00:12:33,462 --> 00:12:34,838
We can do this all day,

184
00:12:35,714 --> 00:12:37,549
so go and get changed now.

185
00:12:37,632 --> 00:12:39,885
Come on. Good boy.

186
00:12:43,763 --> 00:12:44,890
Goodness.

187
00:12:45,515 --> 00:12:48,852
But I think you forgot to do something.

188
00:12:48,935 --> 00:12:49,769
What?

189
00:12:51,354 --> 00:12:52,397
Seriously?

190
00:12:53,398 --> 00:12:54,608
Never mind.

191
00:12:57,736 --> 00:12:58,945
You look great.

192
00:12:59,362 --> 00:13:01,490
I wanted to wear matching sportswear.
Nice.

193
00:13:01,573 --> 00:13:02,991
Why do we need all this?

194
00:13:03,074 --> 00:13:05,494
You can just be around me
in case something happens.

195
00:13:05,577 --> 00:13:08,079
I can't be around you all the time, can I?

196
00:13:08,163 --> 00:13:10,373
And I got fired as your secretary.

197
00:13:10,457 --> 00:13:12,125
I can reinstate you.

198
00:13:12,209 --> 00:13:13,835
So don't worry.

199
00:13:13,919 --> 00:13:17,088
If something does happen
when I'm not around,

200
00:13:17,172 --> 00:13:19,257
I'll turn this whole world upside down.

201
00:13:19,341 --> 00:13:20,926
Why are you being so…

202
00:13:21,676 --> 00:13:23,220
Fine, let's do it.

203
00:13:23,720 --> 00:13:25,305
Before you turn it upside down.

204
00:13:26,723 --> 00:13:29,768
Escaping is
the most important action in a crisis.

205
00:13:29,851 --> 00:13:33,563
Don't try to fight.
Just avoid any conflicts at all costs.

206
00:13:33,647 --> 00:13:34,981
Didn't I tell you?

207
00:13:35,524 --> 00:13:38,944
It's not that I can't fight.
I choose not to.

208
00:13:40,403 --> 00:13:42,489
-Come on.
-You can spar?

209
00:13:42,572 --> 00:13:43,406
Yes.

210
00:13:44,449 --> 00:13:45,617
I won't go easy.

211
00:14:01,424 --> 00:14:04,177
Like I said, it's not that I can't--

212
00:14:07,806 --> 00:14:09,516
When did you get here?

213
00:14:12,352 --> 00:14:13,853
I told you earlier.

214
00:14:13,937 --> 00:14:17,440
Don't try to fight. Escape the situation.

215
00:14:19,276 --> 00:14:20,235
This…

216
00:14:21,570 --> 00:14:23,154
isn't a date.

217
00:14:31,204 --> 00:14:33,999
No wonder he made me stay
with some lousy excuse.

218
00:14:44,050 --> 00:14:46,011
Why on earth are you here?

219
00:14:46,553 --> 00:14:47,971
Were you expecting someone else?

220
00:14:48,054 --> 00:14:49,598
Why are you posing?

221
00:14:49,681 --> 00:14:50,640
It's a turnoff.

222
00:14:54,144 --> 00:14:58,064
Hye-jung, who's pretty at the office
and pretty at someone else's house,

223
00:14:58,148 --> 00:15:00,191
when are you planning to
stop being mad at me?

224
00:15:02,319 --> 00:15:03,403
That day,

225
00:15:05,196 --> 00:15:06,448
when you were in danger,

226
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:08,617
I realized how I felt.

227
00:15:10,118 --> 00:15:11,953
So I'll make the same choice again.

228
00:15:12,412 --> 00:15:14,497
I'll keep anything dangerous hidden away.

229
00:15:15,832 --> 00:15:16,833
I don't want that.

230
00:15:17,250 --> 00:15:20,795
Even if it's for my sake,
I'm sick of being deceived and lied to,

231
00:15:20,879 --> 00:15:22,088
whatever the reason.

232
00:15:25,133 --> 00:15:27,469
It sounds like a conclusion
drawn from experience.

233
00:15:28,553 --> 00:15:29,763
Am I correct?

234
00:15:29,846 --> 00:15:32,807
You're here to pick up the agreement
for the chairman, right?

235
00:15:33,266 --> 00:15:34,934
You can't come in until you answer.

236
00:15:36,102 --> 00:15:37,270
Don't be childish.

237
00:15:37,354 --> 00:15:38,772
No way.

238
00:15:39,481 --> 00:15:41,358
You just need to answer my question.

239
00:15:43,401 --> 00:15:44,402
What if I answer?

240
00:15:46,196 --> 00:15:47,489
Can you even handle it?

241
00:15:50,200 --> 00:15:51,701
SEOUL METROPOLITAN POLICE AGENCY

242
00:15:51,785 --> 00:15:54,996
Kim Hak-ju, the suspect who died.
You know the procedure, right?

243
00:15:56,081 --> 00:15:58,083
Internal Affairs will investigate.

244
00:15:58,166 --> 00:16:00,293
Your team is off the case.

245
00:16:02,754 --> 00:16:04,673
The autopsy report isn't out yet.

246
00:16:04,756 --> 00:16:06,132
Exactly!

247
00:16:06,216 --> 00:16:09,302
If they find evidence
of abuse or negligence in his care,

248
00:16:09,886 --> 00:16:13,598
you won't just be taken off the case.
You'll be suspended.

249
00:16:14,933 --> 00:16:16,184
Get out!

250
00:16:28,697 --> 00:16:30,699
What did the autopsy report say?

251
00:16:30,782 --> 00:16:32,117
It's as expected.

252
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:33,952
Blood tests showed multiple substances,

253
00:16:34,035 --> 00:16:36,454
with the highest concentration
being alprazolam.

254
00:16:36,538 --> 00:16:39,207
He died of an overdose,
whether he did it himself or not.

255
00:16:39,290 --> 00:16:40,291
But…

256
00:16:42,293 --> 00:16:44,003
they don't want me to report it yet.

257
00:16:44,087 --> 00:16:46,339
Seems they'll make you
take the fall big time.

258
00:16:48,550 --> 00:16:49,884
Be careful, okay?

259
00:17:00,019 --> 00:17:02,689
You said you'd go easy.
It still feels sore.

260
00:17:02,772 --> 00:17:05,859
Come on, please don't be mad anymore.
I'll buy you lunch.

261
00:17:05,942 --> 00:17:08,403
-I have something to say after lunch.
-I pick the menu.

262
00:17:08,486 --> 00:17:10,530
But I was going to
choose everything today.

263
00:17:10,613 --> 00:17:12,615
Who knows what else is
on that list of 150?

264
00:17:13,575 --> 00:17:14,868
So you don't want to do them?

265
00:17:14,951 --> 00:17:16,119
It's not that.

266
00:17:17,078 --> 00:17:18,997
But we don't know each other well yet.

267
00:17:19,080 --> 00:17:20,665
Too bad. I already know everything.

268
00:17:22,041 --> 00:17:22,876
I do as well.

269
00:17:23,418 --> 00:17:26,671
But I'm trying to say
that we should take it slow.

270
00:17:26,755 --> 00:17:30,341
If that's the case,
I'll let you choose what we'll eat.

271
00:17:35,472 --> 00:17:36,389
Hold on.

272
00:17:37,140 --> 00:17:39,184
Did you just give me permission?

273
00:17:39,267 --> 00:17:41,394
And I was happy about it.

274
00:17:42,979 --> 00:17:46,024
Everyone in Taekang should've seen this.

275
00:17:46,107 --> 00:17:48,651
Me being on the receiving end
of a power trip.

276
00:17:48,735 --> 00:17:50,403
I should've taken a video.

277
00:17:50,487 --> 00:17:51,446
Dumplings!

278
00:17:57,911 --> 00:17:59,162
Goodness!

279
00:18:00,663 --> 00:18:03,041
-Gosh, Detective--
-Dad!

280
00:18:09,422 --> 00:18:11,466
Can you lower your voice, Dad?

281
00:18:11,549 --> 00:18:13,468
He doesn't know I'm a detective!

282
00:18:13,551 --> 00:18:14,636
Why doesn't he know?

283
00:18:14,719 --> 00:18:17,722
Where else would he find
a great detective girlfriend like you?

284
00:18:18,306 --> 00:18:19,724
Please lower your voice.

285
00:18:19,808 --> 00:18:21,935
Wait, didn't you say
he was getting married?

286
00:18:22,477 --> 00:18:23,478
Is he two-timing?

287
00:18:24,020 --> 00:18:24,896
That little…

288
00:18:24,979 --> 00:18:27,106
Dad.

289
00:18:28,691 --> 00:18:30,318
I'm working undercover.

290
00:18:36,032 --> 00:18:37,283
Undercover?

291
00:18:38,952 --> 00:18:40,995
I was going to tell him,

292
00:18:41,621 --> 00:18:43,456
but things got complicated.

293
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:45,083
So I had no choice.

294
00:18:47,418 --> 00:18:48,419
Jae-hee.

295
00:18:50,255 --> 00:18:53,341
Don't make an excuse
by saying that you have no choice.

296
00:18:54,717 --> 00:18:55,969
In my experience,

297
00:18:56,052 --> 00:18:58,346
nothing good ever comes from that.

298
00:18:58,847 --> 00:19:02,058
You can't make progress
until you resolve your dilemma.

299
00:19:02,642 --> 00:19:03,601
Okay.

300
00:19:06,354 --> 00:19:08,565
Sorry to keep you waiting.

301
00:19:12,986 --> 00:19:13,987
What's with that look?

302
00:19:14,863 --> 00:19:16,656
-Are you embarrassed of me?
-What?

303
00:19:16,739 --> 00:19:18,825
You didn't even let me talk to your dad.

304
00:19:18,908 --> 00:19:21,953
-That's not it.
-You didn't even let me say hello.

305
00:19:22,036 --> 00:19:23,454
Why would I be embarrassed?

306
00:19:23,955 --> 00:19:26,416
My dad is really talkative.
He'll annoy you. That's why--

307
00:19:26,499 --> 00:19:29,127
-You could've at least let me say hello.
-We can do it later.

308
00:19:32,589 --> 00:19:33,423
Why are you back?

309
00:19:35,800 --> 00:19:37,510
So you're the handsome big shot

310
00:19:38,428 --> 00:19:39,470
from that big company,

311
00:19:41,222 --> 00:19:42,515
with money to spare?

312
00:19:44,225 --> 00:19:48,187
The boss who got
my daughter's heart all worked up?

313
00:19:49,606 --> 00:19:51,983
-Why are you making things up?
-All worked up?

314
00:19:52,066 --> 00:19:53,276
Not at all.

315
00:19:57,071 --> 00:19:58,531
Please let me introduce myself.

316
00:20:00,158 --> 00:20:01,451
I'm Yoon Yi-jun.

317
00:20:01,534 --> 00:20:03,745
All right. Then let me warn you.

318
00:20:04,996 --> 00:20:08,249
If you bring tears to Jae-hee's eyes,
you'll cry tears of blood.

319
00:20:10,752 --> 00:20:14,756
I'll upload them to my channel
for everyone to see you cry blood.

320
00:20:15,256 --> 00:20:16,674
I'm that ruthless.

321
00:20:18,927 --> 00:20:19,761
Remember that.

322
00:20:20,261 --> 00:20:21,638
-Yes, sir.
-Go home.

323
00:20:24,849 --> 00:20:25,934
I'm going.

324
00:20:39,614 --> 00:20:41,741
It looks like you grew up
in a loving family.

325
00:20:41,824 --> 00:20:44,243
-What?
-Is that why you turned out so well?

326
00:20:51,334 --> 00:20:52,961
Let's get something to eat.

327
00:20:53,044 --> 00:20:55,421
I know a really good restaurant.

328
00:20:56,464 --> 00:20:57,382
Okay.

329
00:20:59,926 --> 00:21:02,679
KUNMANDU

330
00:21:10,311 --> 00:21:11,145
Here.

331
00:21:11,604 --> 00:21:12,981
The food looks great,

332
00:21:13,064 --> 00:21:16,067
but why did you bring me
to your parents' house without notice?

333
00:21:16,150 --> 00:21:18,695
Did I get prior notice
before being taken to the chairman?

334
00:21:19,821 --> 00:21:23,950
Anyway, you know everything about me now.

335
00:21:24,909 --> 00:21:26,744
That's good and all,

336
00:21:26,828 --> 00:21:28,663
but the eavesdropping is a bit much.

337
00:21:31,124 --> 00:21:33,543
Mom. Dad.

338
00:21:33,960 --> 00:21:35,169
Yes?

339
00:21:37,588 --> 00:21:38,881
Can you please leave?

340
00:21:50,685 --> 00:21:53,021
So you had this every day?

341
00:22:00,778 --> 00:22:02,447
KANG JAE-HEE
POLICE AGENCY

342
00:22:04,032 --> 00:22:07,368
I'm with the Special Investigation Team
at Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency.

343
00:22:13,583 --> 00:22:17,045
We suspected you of being involved
with Han Eun-young's murder.

344
00:22:17,712 --> 00:22:20,089
I approached you undercover
for investigative purposes.

345
00:22:21,174 --> 00:22:22,592
What are you talking about?

346
00:22:24,469 --> 00:22:25,970
After watching you closely,

347
00:22:26,054 --> 00:22:27,805
I realized the culprit was someone else.

348
00:22:27,889 --> 00:22:30,892
From then on,
I protected you as the victim

349
00:22:30,975 --> 00:22:32,268
while gathering information.

350
00:22:35,646 --> 00:22:36,647
I'm sorry.

351
00:22:38,107 --> 00:22:42,487
I lied to you
about both my job and gender.

352
00:22:55,124 --> 00:22:56,542
Wait for me.

353
00:22:59,504 --> 00:23:02,715
You just deceived Taekang, Jae-hee!

354
00:23:03,007 --> 00:23:05,301
This is different
from lying to me about your gender.

355
00:23:05,384 --> 00:23:09,097
This is the last time
I'll ask you for forgiveness.

356
00:23:09,180 --> 00:23:10,681
I know you wanted the killer,

357
00:23:11,682 --> 00:23:13,309
but what if you got caught?

358
00:23:15,394 --> 00:23:16,896
Back then,

359
00:23:17,730 --> 00:23:20,733
I didn't know I'd fall for you like this.

360
00:23:21,192 --> 00:23:24,612
I had no idea I'd find someone
I'd risk everything to protect.

361
00:23:24,695 --> 00:23:26,864
You have a knack for causing a mess.

362
00:23:28,574 --> 00:23:31,077
To be honest,
everything was fake at first.

363
00:23:31,160 --> 00:23:33,037
And I was confused in the process.

364
00:23:33,621 --> 00:23:34,831
Now, everything is real.

365
00:23:35,998 --> 00:23:38,793
I really tried not to like you,
but it didn't work out.

366
00:23:41,337 --> 00:23:44,215
Why would you like me
when you deceived me from the start?

367
00:23:46,008 --> 00:23:48,469
You're the one who liked me first!

368
00:23:48,553 --> 00:23:49,846
You kissed me first!

369
00:23:50,429 --> 00:23:53,558
How could you say that
when you made me fall for you?

370
00:23:54,308 --> 00:23:55,935
You're not in a place to talk back.

371
00:23:57,645 --> 00:24:00,231
I need some time to think.

372
00:24:00,606 --> 00:24:03,025
Go ahead. Take your time.

373
00:24:16,622 --> 00:24:17,832
Take enough time.

374
00:24:17,915 --> 00:24:20,168
How am I supposed to do that

375
00:24:20,251 --> 00:24:21,752
when you're stuck to me like glue?

376
00:24:22,128 --> 00:24:22,962
You're right.

377
00:24:24,297 --> 00:24:25,381
I'll be down here.

378
00:24:27,216 --> 00:24:28,259
Hey!

379
00:24:28,342 --> 00:24:30,303
PERSONNEL FILE

380
00:24:30,386 --> 00:24:31,971
This is nuts.

381
00:24:33,264 --> 00:24:34,307
She's a cop?

382
00:24:35,850 --> 00:24:38,227
Do the police have no moral values?

383
00:24:38,311 --> 00:24:39,687
I knew something was off.

384
00:24:40,062 --> 00:24:41,981
I've never seen anyone refuse money.

385
00:24:42,064 --> 00:24:44,066
I should've known when she did.

386
00:24:44,609 --> 00:24:46,402
Should we run an exclusive in our paper?

387
00:24:47,612 --> 00:24:50,615
We need to blow this wide open
so Yi-jun can't back out.

388
00:24:50,698 --> 00:24:54,327
Then Taekang will also be made a fool of
for not knowing until now.

389
00:24:54,410 --> 00:24:55,411
You're right.

390
00:24:56,204 --> 00:24:58,748
If your dad finds out,
we'll be in trouble too.

391
00:24:58,831 --> 00:25:01,751
We need to find a way
to get someone else to do the dirty work.

392
00:25:08,966 --> 00:25:10,676
CELEBRATING SUPPORT FOR SECOND CHANCES

393
00:25:10,760 --> 00:25:11,886
What?

394
00:25:13,888 --> 00:25:16,098
There are so many interesting photos.

395
00:25:16,515 --> 00:25:18,142
I should've visited sooner.

396
00:25:18,226 --> 00:25:19,560
You should come more often.

397
00:25:20,603 --> 00:25:24,023
Gosh, I should bring tea out for you.

398
00:25:24,106 --> 00:25:26,525
-Let's see.
-I don't want tea.

399
00:25:28,444 --> 00:25:29,570
I want something else.

400
00:25:36,619 --> 00:25:38,412
The retained earnings you stashed away.

401
00:25:40,581 --> 00:25:41,791
Give me half of it.

402
00:25:43,709 --> 00:25:45,795
What are you going on about

403
00:25:45,878 --> 00:25:48,381
after showing up here without notice?

404
00:25:49,215 --> 00:25:53,010
Why do you think Dad is staying silent
about Yi-jun's broken engagement?

405
00:25:54,845 --> 00:25:56,931
He never caused trouble growing up.

406
00:25:57,014 --> 00:25:59,809
But Yi-jun is getting
more and more like your mother.

407
00:26:01,352 --> 00:26:04,647
She was the same in the face of love.
Don't even get me started.

408
00:26:06,023 --> 00:26:08,442
I know what the two of them talked about.

409
00:26:10,152 --> 00:26:12,154
It's obvious what they would talk about.

410
00:26:14,115 --> 00:26:15,324
The company, of course.

411
00:26:15,408 --> 00:26:17,493
My hobby is to collect intel.

412
00:26:18,077 --> 00:26:22,581
Here's the fact.
You took the bait Yi-jun dangled.

413
00:26:23,791 --> 00:26:25,960
He used it to strike a deal with Father.

414
00:26:26,043 --> 00:26:29,922
I heard Yi-jun is looking
into the retained earnings.

415
00:26:30,589 --> 00:26:32,174
I'm proud of him.

416
00:26:33,175 --> 00:26:34,844
If there's an issue, it must be fixed.

417
00:26:35,469 --> 00:26:37,471
I know you're secretly scared to death.

418
00:26:40,308 --> 00:26:43,519
How can you cough up the money
you worked so hard to embezzle?

419
00:26:43,602 --> 00:26:45,980
If it weren't for me,
you'd be six feet under by now.

420
00:26:46,063 --> 00:26:48,816
Yi-jun will have to find a single trace
pointing to me.

421
00:26:48,899 --> 00:26:53,237
That way, no one, including you,
will be disappointed.

422
00:26:54,030 --> 00:26:55,323
Right?

423
00:26:58,909 --> 00:27:01,620
I'll pay a down payment.
I have a conscience, you know.

424
00:27:05,333 --> 00:27:07,209
This is really expensive.

425
00:27:08,252 --> 00:27:09,378
Give it some thought.

426
00:27:11,380 --> 00:27:15,301
With this, you can hand Father
the leash to Yi-jun.

427
00:27:18,763 --> 00:27:19,597
Okay?

428
00:27:32,860 --> 00:27:34,445
POLICE PERSONNEL FILE
KANG JAE-HEE

429
00:27:44,163 --> 00:27:47,249
CHAIRMAN YOON TAE-SIK

430
00:27:47,833 --> 00:27:49,627
Do what you do well.

431
00:27:50,419 --> 00:27:53,339
Turn the tables around first
and then we'll clean up the mess.

432
00:27:55,591 --> 00:27:56,509
Man-seok.

433
00:27:58,928 --> 00:28:00,012
Yes, Tae-sik?

434
00:28:05,601 --> 00:28:06,477
Is it you?

435
00:28:10,481 --> 00:28:11,732
No, sir.

436
00:28:12,900 --> 00:28:15,611
I wouldn't dare to do such a thing.

437
00:28:16,862 --> 00:28:18,989
Yi-jun says he's almost done
looking into it.

438
00:28:19,073 --> 00:28:20,574
He'll eventually find out.

439
00:28:21,992 --> 00:28:23,202
We'll see.

440
00:28:24,120 --> 00:28:25,913
Yes, we will.

441
00:28:31,293 --> 00:28:32,878
I have something urgent to report.

442
00:28:44,348 --> 00:28:45,474
Those darn brats.

443
00:28:50,271 --> 00:28:52,356
There must be an anomaly for a foundation.

444
00:28:52,440 --> 00:28:54,692
If there are identical amounts
at regular intervals,

445
00:28:54,775 --> 00:28:56,444
the money is for a different purpose.

446
00:28:57,736 --> 00:28:59,363
Give me a second, sir.

447
00:29:02,199 --> 00:29:04,827
From the foundation's account
to a personal account…

448
00:29:06,287 --> 00:29:08,330
From the foundation's account to personal?

449
00:29:10,166 --> 00:29:11,125
What?

450
00:29:11,750 --> 00:29:13,252
The access is restricted.

451
00:29:14,920 --> 00:29:17,423
Try bypassing it
using financial institution data.

452
00:29:22,219 --> 00:29:23,179
EXTRA SHOT

453
00:29:24,138 --> 00:29:25,848
Please confirm your order.

454
00:29:26,891 --> 00:29:29,518
I should quit coffee. I really should.

455
00:29:30,811 --> 00:29:31,896
What if I answer?

456
00:29:32,688 --> 00:29:34,231
Can you even handle it?

457
00:29:35,649 --> 00:29:36,734
"I'm in debt."

458
00:29:37,526 --> 00:29:39,278
"Don't worry. I have money."

459
00:29:40,196 --> 00:29:42,448
"I'm married. I have three kids."

460
00:29:42,531 --> 00:29:45,284
No, I doubt that's the case.

461
00:29:46,827 --> 00:29:48,204
"Actually, I'm a man."

462
00:29:49,079 --> 00:29:53,250
There's no way.
Hye-jung is definitely a woman.

463
00:29:56,754 --> 00:29:58,839
-She's pretty.
-Here's your order.

464
00:29:59,590 --> 00:30:00,716
I can handle it.

465
00:30:01,300 --> 00:30:02,635
Yi-jun did it, so why can't I?

466
00:30:10,476 --> 00:30:13,729
I'm ready. I can handle anything.

467
00:30:14,188 --> 00:30:16,524
-The chairman…
-What? The chairman?

468
00:30:17,316 --> 00:30:18,943
Why are you bringing him up?

469
00:30:19,026 --> 00:30:20,945
I don't know if I can handle him.

470
00:30:21,028 --> 00:30:22,196
But please continue.

471
00:30:23,364 --> 00:30:25,324
Apparently, Jae-hee is a cop.

472
00:30:27,535 --> 00:30:29,245
The chairman summoned the two.

473
00:30:29,328 --> 00:30:30,996
She investigated Secretary Han's case.

474
00:30:32,206 --> 00:30:34,792
But deceiving Mr. Yoon about this
is just too much.

475
00:30:36,043 --> 00:30:38,379
Do you think it was wrong of Ms. Kang
to trick him?

476
00:30:40,130 --> 00:30:42,258
From her perspective,
she was only doing her job.

477
00:30:42,883 --> 00:30:45,928
Did you already know about it?

478
00:30:49,223 --> 00:30:51,934
TAEKANG GROUP
CHAIRMAN'S OFFICE

479
00:31:06,657 --> 00:31:10,703
Senior Patrol Officer Kang Jae-hee of
SMPA's Mobile Criminal Investigation Team.

480
00:31:12,913 --> 00:31:14,123
When you take a risk,

481
00:31:14,915 --> 00:31:17,251
you have to anticipate
the worst-case scenario first.

482
00:31:17,751 --> 00:31:19,378
That's the only way to be prepared.

483
00:31:20,671 --> 00:31:21,922
But from what I can tell,

484
00:31:22,673 --> 00:31:23,966
you don't seem prepared.

485
00:31:26,051 --> 00:31:27,344
My father is a businessman.

486
00:31:27,928 --> 00:31:29,346
Think of it as making a deal.

487
00:31:29,847 --> 00:31:31,181
You have to be one step ahead.

488
00:31:31,765 --> 00:31:36,687
THE DAY BEFORE

489
00:31:36,770 --> 00:31:40,441
A mere cop dared to deceive Taekang.

490
00:31:40,983 --> 00:31:42,109
How dare you?

491
00:31:42,192 --> 00:31:43,527
Deceive?

492
00:31:44,278 --> 00:31:48,115
I, your son, wouldn't be standing here
if it weren't for her.

493
00:31:48,616 --> 00:31:49,908
I kept quiet

494
00:31:50,659 --> 00:31:52,369
since it's a family disgrace,

495
00:31:52,453 --> 00:31:55,164
but it's unfair not to brag
about how brilliantly she saved me.

496
00:31:55,247 --> 00:31:56,582
Tell him yourself.

497
00:31:57,291 --> 00:31:58,208
You stay out of this.

498
00:31:58,292 --> 00:32:00,377
I'll call the police commissioner myself.

499
00:32:02,254 --> 00:32:03,130
Sir.

500
00:32:03,797 --> 00:32:06,967
The fact that I saved Mr. Yoon
means he was in danger.

501
00:32:07,051 --> 00:32:09,261
A chandelier with cut wires
fell over his head.

502
00:32:09,928 --> 00:32:11,889
The milk that he drank every day was

503
00:32:11,972 --> 00:32:14,642
laced with herbicide imported
by a Taekang Chemical affiliate.

504
00:32:15,601 --> 00:32:17,895
-Mr. Yoon!
-The car brakes were tampered with,

505
00:32:18,437 --> 00:32:20,147
causing the car accident.

506
00:32:20,230 --> 00:32:22,900
The culprit who was arrested that day
died in custody.

507
00:32:22,983 --> 00:32:24,234
He was murdered.

508
00:32:25,819 --> 00:32:28,072
If you plan to pass Taekang on
to Mr. Yoon,

509
00:32:28,530 --> 00:32:30,240
you need his safety as well.

510
00:32:31,492 --> 00:32:33,911
Don't beat around the bush.
Get to the point!

511
00:32:35,245 --> 00:32:38,207
I'll protect him
while he is handling important matters.

512
00:32:39,208 --> 00:32:41,001
Please let me stay by his side.

513
00:32:43,420 --> 00:32:45,339
That settles what I owe for my son's life.

514
00:32:45,422 --> 00:32:46,924
It's too early to talk settlement.

515
00:32:47,549 --> 00:32:49,593
My proposal was
until the shareholder meeting.

516
00:32:49,677 --> 00:32:50,969
Then bring me results.

517
00:32:51,053 --> 00:32:53,847
Restore everything to the way it was
without any hitch.

518
00:32:54,348 --> 00:32:55,182
Yes, sir.

519
00:32:56,975 --> 00:32:59,687
-Yes, sir.
-I never make a deal at a loss.

520
00:33:02,940 --> 00:33:04,066
You know that, Yi-jun.

521
00:33:06,777 --> 00:33:07,820
Come in.

522
00:33:18,330 --> 00:33:19,665
You were here too, Yi-jun?

523
00:33:31,385 --> 00:33:33,971
Something should have blown up by now.

524
00:33:34,596 --> 00:33:36,140
Why is it so quiet?

525
00:33:36,473 --> 00:33:40,436
EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR YOON NA-JUNG

526
00:33:41,854 --> 00:33:43,605
Did Uncle take the money and run?

527
00:33:50,612 --> 00:33:53,282
Mi-jin, why are you here at this hour?

528
00:33:53,365 --> 00:33:55,576
He wanted to see
the third-quarter performance.

529
00:33:56,535 --> 00:33:57,995
He wants to see the hotel's too?

530
00:33:59,538 --> 00:34:02,332
That, and I just dropped by.

531
00:34:03,792 --> 00:34:06,962
Yi-jun and that secretary
were there earlier.

532
00:34:07,045 --> 00:34:07,880
Really?

533
00:34:08,505 --> 00:34:11,008
Is Father going to kill her?
He went mad, didn't he?

534
00:34:12,176 --> 00:34:13,552
No, not really.

535
00:34:14,511 --> 00:34:17,181
I think Yi-jun convinced Father.

536
00:34:17,264 --> 00:34:18,640
Damn it.

537
00:34:18,724 --> 00:34:20,434
I gave him my support.

538
00:34:20,517 --> 00:34:24,730
I told him to watch for now,
since Yi-jun likes her so much.

539
00:34:25,189 --> 00:34:26,774
Mi-jin!

540
00:34:27,065 --> 00:34:28,901
Are you Mother Teresa or something?

541
00:34:29,526 --> 00:34:32,946
My effort was in vain.
I should've told him to run the exclusive.

542
00:34:33,030 --> 00:34:34,740
What are you plotting now?

543
00:34:34,823 --> 00:34:36,408
None of your business.

544
00:34:38,202 --> 00:34:39,203
Na-jung.

545
00:34:41,371 --> 00:34:42,998
Don't push your luck.

546
00:34:44,792 --> 00:34:45,876
You'll hurt yourself.

547
00:34:47,878 --> 00:34:48,712
What?

548
00:34:50,672 --> 00:34:52,382
Stop making me worry.

549
00:35:07,314 --> 00:35:09,149
The chief secretary told the chairman.

550
00:35:10,275 --> 00:35:12,694
He already had intel on our team.

551
00:35:13,987 --> 00:35:18,242
Thank goodness we told Chairman Yoon
the truth the day before.

552
00:35:19,618 --> 00:35:21,912
I apologize for acting on my own.

553
00:35:21,995 --> 00:35:25,123
Wait, you told him what?

554
00:35:26,208 --> 00:35:29,169
Everything? That you were undercover?
And the investigation?

555
00:35:30,879 --> 00:35:32,339
I had no choice.

556
00:35:40,264 --> 00:35:42,558
You did such a great job.

557
00:35:42,641 --> 00:35:44,643
You really are a heroine.

558
00:35:44,726 --> 00:35:46,395
-I did a good job?
-Of course.

559
00:35:46,478 --> 00:35:48,397
-You just turned yourself in.
-I did well?

560
00:35:48,480 --> 00:35:51,942
But you might get
a lighter sentence for confessing.

561
00:35:52,025 --> 00:35:53,986
Great job.

562
00:35:54,069 --> 00:35:56,613
I can't believe this.

563
00:35:56,697 --> 00:35:58,866
You're the one
who said not to share anything.

564
00:35:58,949 --> 00:36:01,869
I can be very fickle.

565
00:36:01,952 --> 00:36:03,495
We need to survive first.

566
00:36:07,875 --> 00:36:11,545
From what I heard,
nothing is free with Chairman Yoon.

567
00:36:12,045 --> 00:36:14,131
What if he changes his mind later?

568
00:36:14,965 --> 00:36:17,217
We need to find proof
that Na Man-seok is behind it.

569
00:36:18,260 --> 00:36:20,137
How? We lost the authority to investigate.

570
00:36:20,220 --> 00:36:22,055
Right.

571
00:36:22,931 --> 00:36:25,017
That's right.

572
00:36:27,060 --> 00:36:28,478
Good thing you got ahead of him.

573
00:36:28,562 --> 00:36:30,772
Ms. Kang is something else.

574
00:36:30,856 --> 00:36:31,982
She really is.

575
00:36:33,483 --> 00:36:34,985
She's a martial arts expert,

576
00:36:35,068 --> 00:36:38,238
former special forces,
and on the Special Investigation Team.

577
00:36:38,322 --> 00:36:41,825
Don't twist my words
or hear what you want.

578
00:36:41,909 --> 00:36:43,493
This isn't the time to brag.

579
00:36:43,577 --> 00:36:45,537
You're blinded by your love for her.

580
00:36:45,621 --> 00:36:48,874
I wasn't bragging.
I was stating the truth.

581
00:36:48,957 --> 00:36:51,043
Jeez, fine.

582
00:36:51,126 --> 00:36:53,629
But this isn't the time.
The shareholder meeting is soon.

583
00:36:55,923 --> 00:36:57,007
I found a lead.

584
00:36:57,966 --> 00:36:58,967
You found the account?

585
00:36:59,885 --> 00:37:01,303
No wonder you seemed at ease.

586
00:37:01,803 --> 00:37:03,180
You're almost there.

587
00:37:03,764 --> 00:37:06,016
I've dealt with my father all my life.

588
00:37:07,309 --> 00:37:08,602
He's a businessman after all.

589
00:37:09,436 --> 00:37:11,521
But she wasn't intimidated at all.

590
00:37:11,897 --> 00:37:14,608
-Who?
-Kang Jae-hee.

591
00:37:15,067 --> 00:37:17,194
She didn't even bat an eye.

592
00:37:17,277 --> 00:37:20,197
I couldn't be more proud.

593
00:37:20,280 --> 00:37:22,115
Wait, I shouldn't be idling around.

594
00:37:22,199 --> 00:37:23,742
I need to get her something to eat.

595
00:37:25,827 --> 00:37:28,205
Wait, you're actually shopping now?

596
00:37:28,288 --> 00:37:29,289
Beef.

597
00:37:29,915 --> 00:37:32,250
Korean beef. The best quality.

598
00:37:34,169 --> 00:37:36,046
-Doctor Kim.
-How do I add it to my cart?

599
00:37:36,129 --> 00:37:37,756
Do you also do psych?

600
00:37:40,217 --> 00:37:41,093
Sorry.

601
00:37:41,885 --> 00:37:42,928
What took you so long?

602
00:37:43,011 --> 00:37:46,390
Wan-gu goes off on a tangent
every meeting.

603
00:37:47,891 --> 00:37:48,892
What's all this?

604
00:37:49,434 --> 00:37:50,435
You made this yourself?

605
00:37:50,519 --> 00:37:53,772
I told you. It's not that I can't.
I choose not to do things.

606
00:37:56,900 --> 00:37:58,652
Why? Have you fallen for me again?

607
00:37:59,820 --> 00:38:01,697
Look how glowing it is.

608
00:38:03,490 --> 00:38:04,908
I'm talking about the steak.

609
00:38:05,325 --> 00:38:07,369
The color is amazing.

610
00:38:07,452 --> 00:38:08,286
Sit down.

611
00:38:16,169 --> 00:38:17,087
Yi-jun.

612
00:38:18,005 --> 00:38:20,173
-Do you want to get married?
-What?

613
00:38:20,632 --> 00:38:22,676
You're rich, handsome,

614
00:38:22,759 --> 00:38:24,386
and a good cook.

615
00:38:25,012 --> 00:38:26,596
-Jae-hee.
-Yes?

616
00:38:28,807 --> 00:38:30,058
Just eat your steak.

617
00:38:31,435 --> 00:38:32,811
You and your jokes.

618
00:38:33,937 --> 00:38:35,939
-Eat up.
-Okay.

619
00:38:39,568 --> 00:38:40,861
It's so good.

620
00:38:41,737 --> 00:38:44,031
-It's so good!
-Eat a lot.

621
00:38:44,114 --> 00:38:46,074
-There isn't much.
-I made more.

622
00:38:46,158 --> 00:38:48,201
-Really?
-I bought five million won's worth.

623
00:38:50,287 --> 00:38:51,997
You could just give me the money.

624
00:39:01,506 --> 00:39:02,632
What's this?

625
00:39:02,716 --> 00:39:03,884
YI-JUN AND JAE-HEE

626
00:39:04,217 --> 00:39:05,135
Blow the candles.

627
00:39:08,305 --> 00:39:09,139
What?

628
00:39:11,933 --> 00:39:12,851
I won't let you.

629
00:39:22,235 --> 00:39:23,695
You know our captain?

630
00:39:23,779 --> 00:39:26,114
He's just an old man on the outside.

631
00:39:26,198 --> 00:39:27,991
But he's the most experienced.

632
00:39:29,659 --> 00:39:32,954
Wan-gu pretends to be the toughest.

633
00:39:33,038 --> 00:39:34,247
But he's a chicken.

634
00:39:34,331 --> 00:39:36,833
I find that so adorable.

635
00:39:40,337 --> 00:39:41,880
You must care about your team.

636
00:39:41,963 --> 00:39:43,465
Of course.

637
00:39:43,840 --> 00:39:48,178
Those three are just as precious to me
as Sergeant Go is.

638
00:39:49,012 --> 00:39:51,098
Captain, Wan-gu…

639
00:39:51,181 --> 00:39:54,810
Right, Seok-jin graduated
from the police university.

640
00:39:54,893 --> 00:39:58,230
He's the ideal police officer.

641
00:40:01,650 --> 00:40:03,401
But I've made myself perfectly clear.

642
00:40:03,485 --> 00:40:05,612
That he's a great colleague.

643
00:40:05,695 --> 00:40:08,740
But the man that I like is Yoon Yi-jun.

644
00:40:08,824 --> 00:40:11,743
Yoon Yi-jun is my man.

645
00:40:11,827 --> 00:40:12,994
Tell me.

646
00:40:13,870 --> 00:40:15,288
When did you start liking me?

647
00:40:15,956 --> 00:40:16,873
It's been a while.

648
00:40:16,957 --> 00:40:19,084
Was it before or after you pushed me away

649
00:40:19,167 --> 00:40:21,128
with those weird words
on the memorial day?

650
00:40:21,503 --> 00:40:22,337
Before.

651
00:40:25,006 --> 00:40:26,508
Look how pathetic I am,

652
00:40:26,591 --> 00:40:28,218
asking you this question.

653
00:40:31,138 --> 00:40:34,683
You know,
I haven't been so lucky in my life.

654
00:40:35,183 --> 00:40:37,144
But I guess
it was so that I could meet you.

655
00:40:37,227 --> 00:40:39,646
You weren't lucky. You persevered.

656
00:40:40,021 --> 00:40:42,774
-What?
-You fought your way into my world.

657
00:40:43,567 --> 00:40:45,068
And meeting you wasn't luck.

658
00:40:45,443 --> 00:40:47,946
It was a miracle.

659
00:41:18,268 --> 00:41:19,978
I've been called in.

660
00:41:20,770 --> 00:41:22,189
I should get going.

661
00:41:22,272 --> 00:41:23,273
-Really?
-Yes.

662
00:41:24,065 --> 00:41:25,734
-I'll take you.
-No.

663
00:41:26,151 --> 00:41:28,945
It's fine. But let me borrow your car.

664
00:41:29,029 --> 00:41:29,863
Sorry.

665
00:41:30,614 --> 00:41:32,240
I can give you a ride.

666
00:41:32,574 --> 00:41:33,783
I'll call you!

667
00:41:40,498 --> 00:41:43,293
Sir, I've sent you the accounting files.

668
00:41:47,631 --> 00:41:50,133
TAEKANG CULTURAL FOUNDATION
ACCOUNTING MANAGEMENT SYSTEM

669
00:41:53,136 --> 00:41:55,597
ACCOUNT NUMBER

670
00:42:01,478 --> 00:42:02,604
Yes, sir.

671
00:42:02,687 --> 00:42:03,730
I found it.

672
00:42:04,397 --> 00:42:07,317
Compare the retained earnings
and the foundation's cash flow.

673
00:42:07,859 --> 00:42:08,735
Okay.

674
00:42:15,575 --> 00:42:16,701
What was that?

675
00:42:19,412 --> 00:42:21,581
Have you shared your location
with anyone else?

676
00:42:24,626 --> 00:42:26,253
No, sir.

677
00:42:29,089 --> 00:42:30,173
Don't open the door.

678
00:42:31,132 --> 00:42:32,425
I'm on my way there now.

679
00:42:48,984 --> 00:42:51,069
DOOR CAMERA

680
00:42:58,451 --> 00:43:01,413
Bong-yi, why are we the only ones
who got called in?

681
00:43:01,496 --> 00:43:03,123
Is something happening to us?

682
00:43:04,040 --> 00:43:05,667
What? Right now?

683
00:43:06,084 --> 00:43:07,127
Jae-hee is here.

684
00:43:07,210 --> 00:43:08,628
Are you sure it was the bell?

685
00:43:08,712 --> 00:43:12,090
I hid him in a safe place
in case this happened.

686
00:43:12,173 --> 00:43:14,092
It's not a place that'd be easily exposed.

687
00:43:14,592 --> 00:43:16,886
If something happens again because of me…

688
00:43:16,970 --> 00:43:18,096
That won't happen.

689
00:43:22,767 --> 00:43:23,601
Do it.

690
00:43:23,685 --> 00:43:24,519
NA MAN-SEOK

691
00:43:24,978 --> 00:43:25,854
I'll be right there.

692
00:43:25,937 --> 00:43:28,815
-Where…
-Where do you think you're going?

693
00:43:32,610 --> 00:43:34,529
You stubborn idiots.

694
00:43:34,946 --> 00:43:38,408
Hey, do you think
you're in a movie or something?

695
00:43:40,952 --> 00:43:41,828
Undercover?

696
00:43:43,371 --> 00:43:45,081
It's illegal.

697
00:43:45,165 --> 00:43:47,083
It's against regulations!

698
00:43:47,167 --> 00:43:49,002
You ignored the chain of command!

699
00:43:49,085 --> 00:43:51,046
You falsified the operation plan!

700
00:43:52,297 --> 00:43:53,423
Hey.

701
00:43:54,424 --> 00:43:55,467
Hey!

702
00:43:55,550 --> 00:43:58,678
Do you think this is a joke?
Is this your little playground?

703
00:43:59,304 --> 00:44:01,598
Because of you, the whole police force--

704
00:44:01,681 --> 00:44:03,141
What do you think you're doing?

705
00:44:04,642 --> 00:44:06,019
Don't take it out on them.

706
00:44:07,312 --> 00:44:08,563
You can take it out on me.

707
00:44:16,488 --> 00:44:20,116
Be ready for severe disciplinary action
as the officer in charge.

708
00:44:23,953 --> 00:44:27,207
Your team will be disbanded
for this breach.

709
00:44:30,543 --> 00:44:33,880
Everyone stays put until further notice!

710
00:44:35,215 --> 00:44:36,174
Do you understand?

711
00:44:36,925 --> 00:44:38,385
-Damn it.
-Captain!

712
00:44:38,468 --> 00:44:40,136
You and your bullshit.

713
00:44:50,397 --> 00:44:51,940
Park Min-hwan.

714
00:44:52,524 --> 00:44:54,442
You know where he is, don't you?

715
00:44:56,778 --> 00:44:58,738
CALLING

716
00:45:01,825 --> 00:45:05,161
You have 40 minutes.
Take care of him before I arrive.

717
00:45:05,245 --> 00:45:06,663
Don't leave a trace.

718
00:45:21,094 --> 00:45:23,096
The number you've dialed is unavailable.

719
00:45:31,938 --> 00:45:32,897
Where are you going?

720
00:45:32,981 --> 00:45:35,608
The team is disbanded.
We're to stay put, remember?

721
00:45:35,692 --> 00:45:38,069
He'll fall apart
if something happens to Mr. Park.

722
00:45:38,153 --> 00:45:41,448
-He'll blame himself for life. Move.
-Hey, think about yourself first.

723
00:45:42,031 --> 00:45:44,159
Acting recklessly
will get you in deep trouble!

724
00:45:44,242 --> 00:45:46,035
Let me go, Captain.

725
00:45:46,119 --> 00:45:46,953
No!

726
00:45:49,622 --> 00:45:50,540
Isn't this weird?

727
00:45:51,541 --> 00:45:52,709
Why now, of all times?

728
00:45:56,504 --> 00:45:58,173
The chief secretary must've known

729
00:45:58,256 --> 00:45:59,966
that Jae-hee had met the chairman.

730
00:46:00,550 --> 00:46:03,261
We confirmed the connection
between Ma and the chief secretary.

731
00:46:03,344 --> 00:46:06,347
Given his temper,
he would've come after us immediately.

732
00:46:07,474 --> 00:46:09,809
Captain, this was planned.

733
00:46:09,893 --> 00:46:11,978
He'll be in danger at this rate.

734
00:46:12,061 --> 00:46:13,146
Jae-hee.

735
00:46:30,038 --> 00:46:32,040
I told you not to follow us.

736
00:46:32,123 --> 00:46:34,292
I can't cover for you guys,
so you're on your own.

737
00:46:34,375 --> 00:46:36,836
It's not like you ever did.

738
00:46:37,879 --> 00:46:39,172
Go faster!

739
00:46:55,772 --> 00:46:57,106
Manager Park!

740
00:47:07,742 --> 00:47:10,161
Mr. Park! Where are you?

741
00:47:11,996 --> 00:47:13,081
Min-hwan!

742
00:48:10,847 --> 00:48:12,223
You didn't see anything.

743
00:48:14,225 --> 00:48:15,143
It's okay.

744
00:48:57,727 --> 00:48:59,062
I, Na Man-seok,

745
00:48:59,562 --> 00:49:03,566
hereby admit to embezzling
Taekang Group's retained earnings.

746
00:49:04,567 --> 00:49:07,654
I intend to take final responsibility
with this decision.

747
00:49:10,823 --> 00:49:12,450
Why aren't they coming out?

748
00:49:13,785 --> 00:49:17,747
"The assets and documents will be left
in my office at the foundation's."

749
00:49:18,915 --> 00:49:20,917
I'll take the blame,

750
00:49:21,501 --> 00:49:26,422
so for Taekang's sake, I ask that
you bury everything along with me.

751
00:49:26,506 --> 00:49:28,758
"I ask that you bury everything
along with me."

752
00:49:33,096 --> 00:49:35,139
What about the accounting team's manager?

753
00:49:36,140 --> 00:49:37,642
Did he run away with the money?

754
00:49:39,185 --> 00:49:40,436
Father.

755
00:49:44,774 --> 00:49:46,442
Who leaked this to the press?

756
00:49:47,110 --> 00:49:50,655
I told you to keep our family business
within these walls!

757
00:49:53,032 --> 00:49:54,867
I swear it's not us.

758
00:49:55,451 --> 00:49:58,538
You despise it
when people gossip about Taekang.

759
00:49:58,955 --> 00:50:00,415
We have standards too.

760
00:50:01,708 --> 00:50:04,001
You said
you would take care of this quietly.

761
00:50:04,752 --> 00:50:05,962
Is this quiet?

762
00:50:08,673 --> 00:50:09,549
Bring them in.

763
00:50:39,662 --> 00:50:40,705
Father.

764
00:50:40,788 --> 00:50:43,124
Father, we should hold
Uncle's funeral first.

765
00:50:43,207 --> 00:50:44,667
Run the exclusive now.

766
00:50:45,293 --> 00:50:48,421
Cover it up even if you must sell out
these pathetic fools

767
00:50:48,504 --> 00:50:49,797
who dared play Taekang.

768
00:50:52,884 --> 00:50:54,093
I'm sorry, sir.

769
00:50:55,970 --> 00:50:59,015
I've already spoken to the commissioner.

770
00:50:59,098 --> 00:51:01,851
He is also furious,
saying that this illegal investigation

771
00:51:01,934 --> 00:51:04,562
has undermined discipline
within the force.

772
00:51:04,979 --> 00:51:06,981
We have seriously damaged
Taekang's interests

773
00:51:07,398 --> 00:51:09,734
and clearly violated our duties.

774
00:51:09,817 --> 00:51:11,778
The entire team will be dismissed

775
00:51:11,861 --> 00:51:14,363
following the disciplinary procedures.

776
00:51:16,240 --> 00:51:17,158
Sir.

777
00:51:20,453 --> 00:51:21,746
It was me.

778
00:51:21,829 --> 00:51:24,415
I'm the one who forced this investigation.

779
00:51:24,499 --> 00:51:25,708
-Get up.
-Jae-hee.

780
00:51:25,792 --> 00:51:28,169
They all wanted to withdraw,
but I insisted.

781
00:51:28,252 --> 00:51:29,962
I wanted to catch the culprit

782
00:51:30,463 --> 00:51:32,173
and protect Mr. Yoon.

783
00:51:35,384 --> 00:51:37,720
Sir, I'm the captain of the team.

784
00:51:37,804 --> 00:51:39,889
-You--
-Just stay still, please!

785
00:51:40,431 --> 00:51:42,475
Sir, I'm the one who made the decision.

786
00:51:42,558 --> 00:51:44,060
-Are you nuts?
-Detective Kang

787
00:51:44,685 --> 00:51:46,437
only did what I ordered her to do.

788
00:51:46,521 --> 00:51:47,688
It's all my fault.

789
00:51:47,772 --> 00:51:50,650
I sincerely apologize, sir.

790
00:51:51,818 --> 00:51:52,902
I'm sorry, sir.

791
00:51:52,985 --> 00:51:55,154
The others have no reason to be dismissed.

792
00:51:55,238 --> 00:51:59,200
I beg you to ask the commissioner
to rescind the dismissals, sir.

793
00:52:11,587 --> 00:52:12,547
Get up.

794
00:52:13,506 --> 00:52:15,633
Jae-hee, get up!

795
00:52:24,392 --> 00:52:26,561
Do you have to take it this far?

796
00:52:27,728 --> 00:52:28,980
I don't take losses.

797
00:53:41,385 --> 00:53:44,430
You never intended to make an enemy
of the police in the first place.

798
00:53:45,097 --> 00:53:47,099
I know you already had that in mind.

799
00:53:48,309 --> 00:53:50,144
You pressured Jae-hee through dismissals.

800
00:53:50,227 --> 00:53:51,938
You knew that would make me move.

801
00:53:53,522 --> 00:53:55,024
You're beating around the bush.

802
00:53:55,358 --> 00:53:56,442
That position?

803
00:53:56,901 --> 00:54:01,113
The tragedy that began
because of that so-called great position.

804
00:54:01,822 --> 00:54:03,240
It needs to end now.

805
00:54:04,867 --> 00:54:06,035
Does it?

806
00:54:07,370 --> 00:54:08,371
I admit.

807
00:54:08,454 --> 00:54:10,164
I fell short this time.

808
00:54:11,165 --> 00:54:12,500
I lost Park Min-hwan,

809
00:54:13,209 --> 00:54:15,419
and I can't even guess
who else is involved.

810
00:54:16,462 --> 00:54:18,631
That means everyone around me is in danger

811
00:54:19,006 --> 00:54:21,217
and that no one can stay by my side.

812
00:54:25,972 --> 00:54:27,264
Withdraw the dismissals

813
00:54:28,599 --> 00:54:29,433
of the detectives.

814
00:54:31,394 --> 00:54:32,979
I will ensure you take no loss.

815
00:55:18,899 --> 00:55:20,234
You've done great work.

816
00:55:22,319 --> 00:55:23,320
Thank you, ma'am.

817
00:55:34,123 --> 00:55:36,042
The number you've dialed is…

818
00:55:45,926 --> 00:55:47,928
You weren't picking up, so I was worried.

819
00:55:48,888 --> 00:55:50,264
I have something to tell you.

820
00:55:52,641 --> 00:55:54,310
Yes, go ahead.

821
00:55:55,102 --> 00:55:56,145
Let's end it here.

822
00:56:00,566 --> 00:56:01,984
What do you mean?

823
00:56:02,610 --> 00:56:04,320
If your team ends up forced to resign,

824
00:56:05,321 --> 00:56:07,448
could you stand
being resented by them forever?

825
00:56:08,449 --> 00:56:10,201
You're already struggling.

826
00:56:10,993 --> 00:56:12,870
I'm sure we can find a way.

827
00:56:12,953 --> 00:56:14,413
-If we--
-What about me?

828
00:56:14,789 --> 00:56:17,083
Should I feel bad for you
for the rest of my life?

829
00:56:17,541 --> 00:56:19,251
What am I supposed to do?

830
00:56:19,335 --> 00:56:22,338
I never asked to be born
into this family and these circumstances.

831
00:56:22,421 --> 00:56:23,714
What if I still choose you

832
00:56:25,341 --> 00:56:27,051
despite all of that?

833
00:56:35,476 --> 00:56:38,020
You can't turn your back on them
like that.

834
00:56:38,646 --> 00:56:40,064
I know you.

835
00:56:40,648 --> 00:56:41,816
But instead,

836
00:56:42,900 --> 00:56:44,777
you'll be the one I'm turning my back on.

837
00:56:52,576 --> 00:56:53,869
We'll get used to it.

838
00:56:55,746 --> 00:56:56,956
It'll get easier.

839
00:57:00,334 --> 00:57:02,545
So go back to where you should be.

840
00:57:03,546 --> 00:57:05,256
I'll find my own place too.

841
00:57:08,342 --> 00:57:09,260
Jae-hee.

842
00:57:13,305 --> 00:57:14,140
Take care.

843
00:57:18,769 --> 00:57:19,937
"Take care"?

844
00:57:21,230 --> 00:57:22,523
Is this really it?

845
00:57:24,358 --> 00:57:25,651
Is this how we end things?

846
00:57:28,112 --> 00:57:30,531
After everything it took to be with you?

847
00:57:30,614 --> 00:57:33,117
I won't avoid or hide anymore.

848
00:57:35,828 --> 00:57:37,121
Have a good life.

849
00:57:41,000 --> 00:57:43,377
Don't do this. Don't go.

850
00:57:43,878 --> 00:57:44,879
Yi-jun!

851
00:58:02,188 --> 00:58:03,439
Don't go.

852
00:59:04,959 --> 00:59:06,877
SPECIAL THANKS TO KIM DO-YOON,
PARK JUN-MUYN, AND JUNG YOO-MIN

853
00:59:10,965 --> 00:59:13,133
-I broke up with her.
-I miss her.

854
00:59:13,217 --> 00:59:16,637
It's the first time I've loved someone.
I don't know how to break up.

855
00:59:16,720 --> 00:59:17,763
We're nothing now.

856
00:59:17,846 --> 00:59:19,515
Even if I do this?
Your heart is about to burst.

857
00:59:19,598 --> 00:59:21,767
My existence is a danger to her.

858
00:59:21,850 --> 00:59:24,353
I'd like to request your cooperation
with a special investigation.

859
00:59:24,436 --> 00:59:26,313
If it's going to crumble
over something like this…

860
00:59:26,397 --> 00:59:27,606
They'll make a move.

861
00:59:27,690 --> 00:59:29,108
Did he tell you to keep me here?

862
00:59:29,191 --> 00:59:30,776
-Last chance?
-Last chance to remove me.

863
00:59:30,859 --> 00:59:33,028
We sincerely cared for

864
00:59:33,112 --> 00:59:34,822
and loved each other.

865
00:59:34,905 --> 00:59:38,993
Jae-hee. How about we meet like that
in our next lives?

866
00:59:42,496 --> 00:59:45,499
Translated by Leo Chung
